+## 0. Baseline score (production, before these changes)
+
+`scripts/seo-audit.ts --base https://nxeon.cloud --per-template 15` on 2026-10-01 (158 pages sampled of 66,281 sitemap URLs; the site score weights each template by its share of the sitemap, so the 64,856-URL mod template dominates it):
+
+| template | sitemap URLs | sampled | avg score | main deductions |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| game-location | 615 | 15 | **80.8** | title-long, desc-long, near-duplicate (15/15) |
+| blog-index | 1 | 1 | 85 | JSON-LD missing url, og:image |
+| location-landing | 162 | 15 | 91.6 | og:image, title/description length |
+| blog-post | 346 | 15 | 92.4 | Organization without url (15/15) |
+| static | 19 | 15 | 93.7 | og:image (13/15) |
+| mod | 64,856 | 15 | 94.5 | image width/height (15/15) |
+| product | 17 | 15 | 94.9 | og:image (15/15), short titles |
+| game-landing | 65 | 15 | 95.1 | description length |
+| tool / comparison | 16 / 39 | 15 / 15 | 96.3 / 96.5 | og:image (15/15) |
+| game-region | 141 | 15 | 98.3 | description length |
+
+Site score **94.4 / 100**. The score is a hygiene score (does each page carry the right tags); it deliberately cannot see ranking quality, which is why §4 matters more than the number. The near-duplicate cluster is the one thing it ranks as the worst template.
